\title{ggpointless: Extra Geometries and Stats for 'ggplot2'}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Provides additional geometries and statistical layers for 'ggplot2'. Includes visual-effect geoms built on 'grid' linear and radial gradients and Porter-Duff compositing — faded areas, paths, bars, rectangles, and ridgelines, plus points with a glow — alongside mathematically driven layers such as catenary curves, Chaikin's corner-cutting smoothing, and truncated Fourier-series reconstruction. Also ships Lexis diagrams, selective highlighting of extreme and first / last observations, unit (isotype) bar charts, and grid lines that draw above other layers.
